meta {
  name: current stock report
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}reports/current-stock/
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~export: csv
  ~category: 1
  ~search: motor
  ~p: 1
  ~page_size: 25
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  Every non-archived component with category, unit, total quantity, chambers
  held, last buying price, delivery charge and estimated stock value. Admin or
  Manager. Filters: `category`, `search` (name or part number). `summary` has
  the component count and total estimated stock value (indicative only, not
  an accounting figure).

  Like every report (FR-9.1): a paginated JSON table with `columns` (key and header)
  and, where it applies, a `summary`. Add `?export=xlsx` or `?export=csv` to download
  the whole report (every page) as a file; quantities are written with their unit symbol.

  ## API example response
  {
    "count": 8,
    "page_size": 25,
    "next": null,
    "previous": null,
    "num_pages": 1,
    "current_page": 1,
    "results": [
